# OCO Trailer Rentals — environment settings
#
# Copy this file to `.env` for local development, and set the same two values in
# Vercel under Project Settings → Environment Variables (all environments).
#
# Both values below are browser-safe by design. The publishable key identifies the
# project; it grants no access on its own — every table is protected by Postgres
# row-level security, which is what actually decides who can read or write what.
#
# NEVER put the Supabase service-role key here, or anywhere else in this repo.
# It bypasses row-level security entirely. Server-only secrets (service role,
# Stripe secret key, Stripe webhook signing secret) belong in Supabase Edge
# Function secrets, never in a VITE_ variable — anything prefixed VITE_ is
# compiled into the JavaScript that ships to every visitor's browser.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=your-publishable-or-anon-key

# Stripe. The publishable key is browser-safe — it can only create payment
# intents that the server has already authorised, and it is visible in the
# page source of every Stripe checkout on the internet.
#
# The SECRET key and the WEBHOOK SIGNING SECRET are not set here. They belong in
# Supabase → Edge Functions → Secrets, as STRIPE_SECRET_KEY and
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET. Card payment stays switched off until they are set, and
# the checkout says so rather than pretending to take a card.
VITE_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_live_or_pk_test_key
